With these two changes:

- As soon as the input inside NumberPicker receives focus, `hasFocused` is set to `true`.
- Our wrapper’s class list now includes `-show-trigger` whenever `hasFocused` is `true` (or `alwaysShowTrigger` was already `true`), so the up/down controls will become visible on keyboard focus.
- When the picker blurs, `hasFocused` goes back to `false` and the buttons hide again (unless `alwaysShowTrigger` is on).
